From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Ollis <plicease@cpan.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Compile against libc16 and libkitchen16 (M3.4)

perl16's runtime build (P16_RT) compiles these sources against libc16's
and libkitchen16's headers, force-including msdos/p16rt.h, and links
their libraries in place of Open Watcom's runtime (perl16 #16, #17;
docs/M3-RUNTIME-AUDIT.md, sections 5.3, 6 and 7). The development build
keeps Open Watcom's runtime.

- cmd.c, util.c: deb(), fatal() and warn() use <stdarg.h> instead of
  <varargs.h>, which libc16 doesn't have, with the prototypes perl.h
  already gives them; mess() takes the format as a parameter.
- util.c: no K&R malloc() and realloc() declarations under P16_RT, where
  <stdlib.h> declares them returning void *. setenv() passed strupr()
  two arguments; it takes one.
- dolist.c, stab.c, msdos/popen.c: the functions the library calls back
  (qsort, signal, atexit) are P16_CB, which is __cdecl under P16_RT.
- perly.c: libc16 has no stdaux or stdprn stream to close. main()
  takes two parameters under P16_RT and env is a local: libc16's startup
  passes two with SP at the end of the program's memory block, so
  assigning a third parameter overwrote DOS's next memory control block.
- msdos/msdos.c: under P16_RT, ioctl() maps a DOS error as libc16 does
  (its docs/spec/io.md), which has no EPERM, ENFILE or EZERO, and
  do_aspawn() and do_spawn() give children environ, since libc16's
  spawnvp() and spawnl() pass DOS's environment rather than %ENV. The
  shell's command goes through libc16_systeme() (libc16 0.15), which
  passes it to COMSPEC /C byte for byte with environ. A command run
  directly is split as libc16's startup splits a command tail, double
  quotes and backslashes included, so that, quoted again by
  spawnvpe(), the program sees the arguments the command names.
- msdos/popen.c: the temporary file is created exclusively in TEMP, TMP
  or the current directory by perl16_etemp() (msdos/etemp.c), instead of
  named by tempnam(), which libc16 doesn't have and which only checks
  that a name is free (docs/M2-REPORT.md, section 12).
---
diff --git a/cmd.c b/cmd.c
--- a/cmd.c
+++ b/cmd.c
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@
 #include "perl.h"
 
